      "lineNbr": 155,
      "author": {
        "id": 1135107
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-17T22:25:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You mean the race condition between determining the open port and using it?\n\nI debug-logged this and it seems like the system doesn\u0027t reuse these ports (at least not right away) - it just goes one by one from some high number in the second half of the uint32 range. And the second half of the port range is kind-of reserved (not formally, I guess?) for automatic assignment, so unless some other process hand-picks a number from the high range, there won\u0027t be any conflicts.\n\nI would say it would not fail when run concurrently at all. But up to you if you want to add API for automatic port assignment?",
      "parentUuid": "cec77d83_0048cc12",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 155,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 155,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "ea84289d64d0e7aab32a9d2d92dbd3101947d4bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
